  </mj-head>
  <mj-body width="648px" background-color="#505050">
    <mj-section padding="0px 0px 30px" background-color="#191919">
      <mj-column padding="0px">
        <mj-image
          src="https://demo.react.email/static/codepen-challengers.png"
          alt="codepen"
          width="600px"
          align="center"
          padding="0px"
        />
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>
    <mj-section padding="0px">
      <mj-column padding="0px">
        <mj-text
          padding="10px 0px 16px"
          font-size="13px"
          line-height="1.5"
          align="center"
          css-class="community-rich-0"
          ><a>View this Challenge on CodePen</a>
        </mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>
    <mj-section padding="30px" background-color="#f0d361">
      <mj-column padding="0px">
        <mj-text padding="0px" font-size="24px" line-height="1.3" font-weight="400"
          ><strong>This week:</strong> #CodePenChallenge:</mj-text
        >
        <mj-text padding="4px 0px 0px" font-size="32px" line-height="1.5">Cubes</mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>
    <mj-section padding="16px 24px 0px" background-color="#ffffff">
      <mj-column padding="0px">
        <mj-text padding="0px 0px 16px" font-size="16px" line-height="1.5"
          >The Shape challenge continues!</mj-text
        >
        <mj-text
          padding="0px 0px 16px"
          font-size="16px"
          line-height="1.5"
          css-class="community-rich-1"
          >Last week, we kicked things off with round shapes. We "rounded" up the Pens from week one
          in our <a>#CodePenChallenge: Round</a> collection.</mj-text
        >
        <mj-text padding="0px 0px 16px" font-size="16px" line-height="1.5"
          >This week, we move on to cubes 🧊</mj-text
        >
        <mj-text padding="0px 0px 16px" font-size="16px" line-height="1.5"
          >Creating cubes in the browser is all about mastery of illusion. Take control of
          perspective and shadows and you can make the magic of 3D on a flat screen 🧙</mj-text
        >
        <mj-text padding="0px 0px 16px" font-size="16px" line-height="1.5"
          >This week is a fun chance to work on your CSS shape-building skills, or dig into a 3D
          JavaScript library like Three.js.</mj-text
        >
        <mj-text padding="0px 0px 16px" font-size="16px" line-height="1.5"
          >This week's starter template features an ice cube emoji to help inspire a "cool" idea for
          your Pen. As always, the template is just a jumping off point. Feel free to incorporate
          the 🧊 in your creation, add more elements, or freeze it out completely and start over
          from scratch!</mj-text
        >
        <mj-text
          padding="20px"
          font-size="16px"
          line-height="1.5"
          css-class="codepen-challenge community-rich-2"
          >💪 <strong>Your Challenge:</strong> <a>create a Pen that includes cube shapes.</a>
        </mj-text>
        <mj-spacer height="40px" />
        <mj-image
          src="https://demo.react.email/static/codepen-cube.png"
          alt="codepen"
          width="600px"
          align="left"
          padding="0px"
        />
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>
    <mj-wrapper padding="40px 24px 24px" background-color="#ffffff">
      <mj-section padding="35px 20px 30px" border="6px solid #2138c6" background-color="#0b112a">
        <mj-column padding="0px">
          <mj-image
            src="https://demo.react.email/static/codepen-pro.png"
            alt="codepen"
            width="250px"
            align="center"
            padding="0px 0px 30px"
          />
          <mj-text
            padding="0px 0px 16px"
            font-size="14px"
            line-height="1.5"
            align="center"
            color="#ffffff"
            >CodePen PRO combines a bunch of features that can help any front-end designer or
            developer at any experience level.</mj-text
          >
          <mj-button
            align="center"
            padding="0px"
            inner-padding="12px"
            border-radius="4px"
            font-size="15px"
            background-color="#2138c6"
            color="#ffffff"
            font-weight="700"
            line-height="18px"
            >Learn More</mj-button
          >
        </mj-column>
      </mj-section>
    </mj-wrapper>
    <mj-section padding="30px" background-color="#f5d247">
      <mj-column padding="0px">
        <mj-text padding="0px" font-size="18px" line-height="1.5" css-class="community-rich-3"
          ><strong>To participate:</strong> <a>Create a Pen →</a> and tag it
          <a><strong>codepenchallenge</strong></a> and <a><strong>cpc-cubes</strong></a
          >. We'll be watching and gathering the Pens into a Collection, and sharing on
          <a>Twitter</a> and <a>Instagram</a> (Use the #CodePenChallenge tag on Twitter and
          Instagram as well).</mj-text
        >
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>
    <mj-section padding="0px 14px" background-color="#ffffff">
      <mj-column padding="0px 10px" width="50%">
        <mj-text padding="16px 0px" font-size="18px" line-height="1.1" font-weight="900"
          >IDEAS!</mj-text
        >
        <mj-text
          padding="20px"
          font-size="13px"
          line-height="1.5"
          container-background-color="#fff4c8"
          css-class="codepen-card-idea community-rich-8"
          ><em>🌟</em><br />This week we move from 2 dimensions to three! Maybe you could exercise
          your <a>perspective</a> in CSS to create a 3D cube. Or, you can try out creating 3D shapes
          in JavaScript, using <a>WebGL</a> or building a <a>Three.js scene</a>.</mj-text
        >
        <mj-spacer height="20px" />
        <mj-text
          padding="20px"
          font-size="13px"
          line-height="1.5"
          container-background-color="#fff4c8"
          css-class="codepen-card-idea community-rich-12"
          ><em>🌟</em><br />There's more to cubes than just six square sides. There are variations
          on the cube that could be fun to play with this week: <a>cuboid shapes</a> are hexahedrons
          with faces that aren't always squares. And if you want to really push the boundaries of
          shape, consider the 4 dimensional <a>tesseract!</a>
        </mj-text>
        <mj-spacer height="20px" />
        <mj-text
          padding="20px"
          font-size="13px"
          line-height="1.5"
          container-background-color="#fff4c8"
          css-class="codepen-card-idea community-rich-15"
          ><em>🌟</em><br />Here's a mind-bending idea that can combine the round shapes from week
          one with this week's cube theme: <a>Spherical Cubes</a> 😳 Solving longstanding
          mathematical mysteries is probably outside the scope of a CodePen challenge, but you could
          use front-end tools to explore fitting spheres into cubes, or vice-versa.</mj-text
        >
        <mj-spacer height="20px" />
      </mj-column>
      <mj-column padding="0px 10px" width="50%">
        <mj-text padding="16px 0px" font-size="18px" line-height="1.1" font-weight="900"
          >RESOURCES!</mj-text
        >
        <mj-text
          padding="20px"
          font-size="13px"
          line-height="1.5"
          container-background-color="#d9f6ff"
          css-class="codepen-card-resource community-rich-17"
          ><em>📖</em><br />Learn all about <a>How CSS Perspective Works</a> and how to build a 3D
          CSS cube from scratch in Amit Sheen's in-depth tutorial for CSS-Tricks. Or, check out
          stunning examples of WebGL cubes from Matthias Hurrle: <a>Just Ice</a> and
          <a>Posing</a>.</mj-text
        >
        <mj-spacer height="20px" />
        <mj-text
          padding="20px"
          font-size="13px"
          line-height="1.5"
          container-background-color="#d9f6ff"
          css-class="codepen-card-resource community-rich-21"
          ><em>📖</em><br />Want to go beyond the square cube? Draw inspiration from
          EntropyReversed's <a>Pulsating Tesseract</a>, Josetxu's <a>Rainbow Cuboid Loader</a>, or
          Ana Tudor's <a>Pure CSS cuboid jellyfish</a>.</mj-text
        >
        <mj-spacer height="20px" />
        <mj-text
          padding="20px"
          font-size="13px"
          line-height="1.5"
          container-background-color="#d9f6ff"
          css-class="codepen-card-resource community-rich-25"
          ><em>📖</em><br />Did that spherical cubes concept pique your interest? Explore Ryan
          Mulligan's <a>Cube Sphere</a>, Munir Safi's
          <a>3D Sphere to Cube Animation With Virtual Trackball</a> and Ana Tudor's
          <a>Infinitely unpack prism</a> for more mindbending cube concepts that test the boundaries
          of how shapes interact with each other.</mj-text
        >
        <mj-spacer height="20px" />
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>
    <mj-section padding="40px 0px 120px">
      <mj-column padding="0px">
        <mj-button
          align="center"
          padding="0px"
          inner-padding="15px 30px"
          border-radius="4px"
          font-size="26px"
          background-color="#222222"
          color="#1155cc"
          font-weight="700"
          >Go to Challenge Page</mj-button
        >
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>
    <mj-section padding="0px 24px" background-color="#ffffff">
      <mj-column padding="0px">
        <mj-text
          padding="16px 0px"
          font-size="13px"
          line-height="1.5"
          color="#505050"
          css-class="community-rich-29"
          >You can adjust your <a>email preferences</a> any time, or <a>instantly opt out</a> of
          emails of this kind. Need help with anything? Hit up <a>support</a>.</mj-text
        >
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>
    <mj-section padding="0px">
      <mj-column padding="0px">
        <mj-spacer height="48px" />
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>
  </mj-body>
</mjml>
